  "notes": "Transcribed from the official SCC 'International Studies A.A. Degree - Local GE' program map, Catalog 2026-27, published August 15, 2026 (mapmaker.losrios.edu/Maps/7495/PublishedPdf). GE Pattern: SCC Local GE. Official Total Units: 60.5-65; this seed models the first-listed/recommended low path = 16 + 16 + 15 + 13.5 = 60.5 units (ENGL C1000 at 3 units per the official SCC English course page; IS 494 at 0.5 units, the low end of the 0.5-4 range). Semester sums verified against the map's 16-17 / 16 / 15 / 13.5-17 headers. 4 terms (within the AA/AS 4-7 gate). Distinct from map 7776 (sacramento-city-college-aa-international-studies), which is the Cal-GETC GE version of the same program. Major Elective (documented): minimum 8 units of Foreign Language from ARABIC 401 & 402, CANT 401/402/411/412, FREN 401/402/411/412, GREEK 401 & 402, ITAL 401 & 402, JAPAN 401/402/411/412, KOREAN 401 & 402, MAND 401/402/411/412, PRSIAN 401 & 402, PNJABI 401 & 402, RUSS 401/402/411/412, TGLG 401 & 402, VIET 401 & 402 (choose 4 units in Sem 1 and 4 units in Sem 2 in the SAME language). Sem 1: ARABIC 401 selected (first-listed, 4 units). Sem 2: ARABIC 402 selected (same-language continuation, 4 units; prerequisite: ARABIC 401 with 'C' or better, or two years HS, or instructor permission). Language prerequisites documented: 402 level requires 401 with 'C' or better (or 2 yrs HS or permission); 411 requires 402 with 'C' or better (or 3 yrs HS or permission); 412 requires 411 with 'C' or better (or 4 yrs HS or permission). ME total: ARABIC 401 (4) + ARABIC 402 (4) = 8 units. Choice slots: (1) GE ENGL C1000 / ENGL 488 / ESLW 340, SCC Local Area L1A — ENGL C1000 selected (3 units); (2) GE INDIS 313 / HCD 310, Life Development Skills, SCC Local Area L7B — INDIS 313 selected (first-listed; first-time FYE students take INDIS 313); (3) ME ANTH 310 / ANTH 481H, Cultural Anthropology — ANTH 310 selected (first-listed, 3 units); (4) ME POLS 310 / POLS 480H, Introduction to International Relations — POLS 310 selected (first-listed, 3 units); (5) ME HIST C1002 / HIST C1002H, History of the United States (1865-Present), SCC Local Area L4 — HIST C1002 selected (first-listed, 3 units). GE Mathematical Concepts and Quantitative Reasoning (SCC Local Area L2): choose one recommended course under SLAM - Statistics and Liberal Arts Math placements (check eServices). ECON C2002 prerequisite: placement via multiple measures or completion of elementary algebra or higher. IS 494 Topics in International Studies (0.5-4 units) modeled at 0.5 units. Electives: any courses numbered 100-499 (see a counselor). AA/AS requirements: 60 degree-applicable units with 2.0 GPA, 12 units within Los Rios, each required course 'C' or better, SCC Local GE Areas L1A-L7B. Bachelor's-degree holders are deemed to have satisfied GE (per map). International Studies, People & Society Meta Majors.",
